                        "entry_id": "fc2c91b8-5f86-370a-8d4b-2458711b85d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "starke Verliebtheit"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d9f6246-8cc2-4a97-ae59-c755996978b3",
                                "sense_id": "0a79c8f2-d494-3482-b624-2fff877cde50",
                                "text": "„Diesen Zustand extremer, obsessiver Verliebtheit, der über das normale Kribbeln im Bauch hinausgeht, nennen Psychologen Limerenz.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bf5e8026-7a6b-46c8-9601-141841130f40",
                        "source_entry_id": "fc2c91b8-5f86-370a-8d4b-2458711b85d8",
                        "source_sense_id": "0a79c8f2-d494-3482-b624-2fff877cde50",
                        "source_sense_description": "Psychologie: starke Verliebtheit",
                        "target_lang_word": "limerence",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "limerence",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac5fcd68-d4e6-3e89-941b-151f30ab3be3",
                                        "entry_id": "5c2595cb-b2e3-3571-ba55-59534fd557e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An involuntary romantic infatuation with another person, especially combined with an overwhelming, obsessive need to have one's feelings reciprocated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3af3aa7f-a1d1-4b7b-a105-152088eeb945",
                                                "sense_id": "ac5fcd68-d4e6-3e89-941b-151f30ab3be3",
                                                "text": "I first used the term ‘amorance’ then changed it back to ‘limerence’ […]. It has no roots whatsoever. It looks nice. It works well in French. Take it from me it has no etymology whatsoever."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9895ff80-c0d4-474d-ba4e-96364832659c",
                                                "sense_id": "ac5fcd68-d4e6-3e89-941b-151f30ab3be3",
                                                "text": "When someone is under the spell of limerence, not even being rejected dampens down the madness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05db0f61-e76f-488c-b8a6-2150f0f754f1",
                                                "sense_id": "ac5fcd68-d4e6-3e89-941b-151f30ab3be3",
                                                "text": "But limerence, lovely as it feels, is a time-limited event—it lasts about five years for most couples."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6856ad1e-813d-42d6-8d75-8bcc8b45fe82",
                                                "sense_id": "ac5fcd68-d4e6-3e89-941b-151f30ab3be3",
                                                "text": "Limerence is a state of overwhelming and unexpected longing for emotional reciprocation from another human, known as a limerent object (LO), who is often perceived as perfect but unavailable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c7452880-8a44-4c49-bc36-aa2f6e5f3509",
                        "source_entry_id": "fc2c91b8-5f86-370a-8d4b-2458711b85d8",
                        "source_sense_id": "0a79c8f2-d494-3482-b624-2fff877cde50",
                        "source_sense_description": "Psychologie: starke Verliebtheit",
                        "target_lang_word": "limérence",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "limérence",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e226c66-c5ac-3ca7-9765-c6ea953ab02a",
                                        "entry_id": "f4e346ec-f70e-3d6f-a8e3-72e265041001",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "État d'esprit involontaire d'un individu très amoureux, qui se caractérise par un puissant désir de réciprocité des sentiments, impliquant des pensées intrusives, obsessionnelles et compulsives."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Anglicism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "163f2b6f-a288-4ed6-8c5a-e50a7d34c86c",
                                                "sense_id": "2e226c66-c5ac-3ca7-9765-c6ea953ab02a",
                                                "text": "« Un seul être vous manque, et tout est dépeuplé », disait dans son ouvrage L’isolement le poète Alphonse de Lamartine. Quoi de plus précis que cette célèbre citation pour qualifier le terme de « limérence » ?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
